; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wyoming is the most Republican-leaning state in the country, and the 2028 presidential race there is expected to follow that pattern. The incumbent president is term-limited, so both parties will nominate new candidates, but the state's R+23 partisan baseline gives the Republican nominee an enormous structural advantage regardless of who runs.\n\nNo Wyoming-specific polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market prices are available for this race, so the forecast rests on fundamentals alone. The state has backed Republicans by wide margins in every recent presidential election, and there is no evidence of a competitive Democratic operation here. The Republican nominee is a heavy favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0282, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0274, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0279, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0258, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0202, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0264, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0221, "margin": -23.0}]}